{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"e50b3cba03cb8eee","type":"group","x":-2800,"y":280,"width":2120,"height":2440,"label":"Phases"},
		{"id":"669d4455ba87a8d9","type":"group","x":-135,"y":347,"width":291,"height":793,"label":"HITL Flow"},
		{"id":"b680dc23adb63100","type":"text","text":"**Metadata** ","x":-290,"y":-251,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4be6d60609ac238d","type":"text","text":"Inferred Metadata","x":-290,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b79e4e06a5dd76b2","type":"text","text":"**No HITL**","x":-560,"y":140,"width":120,"height":60},
		{"id":"f38177e272ee71ee","type":"text","text":"**HITL kicks in** ","x":100,"y":140,"width":140,"height":60},
		{"id":"05201613ec1c136e","type":"text","text":"Reinfer entire metadata","x":260,"y":367,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"efb742f611a3a9fd","type":"text","text":"User review metadata","x":-100,"y":367,"width":220,"height":53},
		{"id":"537d093ac122f3c0","type":"text","text":"Identifies Issues","x":-115,"y":460,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"622857ee9c0c3c4c","type":"text","text":"Makes Correction","x":-114,"y":560,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"07c8d86f722ab89f","type":"text","text":"System Validates","x":-114,"y":660,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"2d7c1c0ee5815ff8","type":"text","text":"Calculates Impact","x":-114,"y":760,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"975321c0ee87fe48","type":"text","text":"Re-inference Process","x":-115,"y":860,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"fcf512cbc399a7a0","type":"text","text":"Updated Metadata","x":-114,"y":960,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e1ff5f7035677642","type":"text","text":"User Confirms Changes\n","x":-115,"y":1060,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4995ffddde1a27cf","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 3: Multi-Layer Validation**\n\n### **Layer 1: Structural Validation** (Ring 1 - Physical Reality)\n\n**Question**: Does column `ledger_id` exist in `GENERAL_LEDGER` table?\n\n**Validation Sources**:\n\n- Query MongoDB column metadata for this table\n- Check freshness: When was schema last scanned?\n- Cross-reference with actual database (optional, based on recency)\n\n**Possible Outcomes**:\n\n**Outcome A: Column Exists**\n\n- ✅ Proceed to next validation layer\n- Log: User correction appears valid\n\n**Outcome B: Column Does NOT Exist**\n\n- ❌ Block with error\n- Show available columns\n- Offer fuzzy matching: \"Did you mean `ledger_line_id`?\"\n- Provide options:\n    - Select from dropdown of actual columns\n    - Explain why `ledger_id` is needed (capture intent)\n    - Request schema refresh (maybe schema is stale)\n\n**Outcome C: Uncertain (Schema data stale)**\n\n- ⚠️ Show warning: \"Schema last scanned 3 days ago, column may or may not exist\"\n- Offer to refresh schema first\n- Allow proceeding with acknowledgment of risk\n\n---\n\n### **Layer 2: Data Quality Validation** (Ring 2 - Best Practices)\n\nAssuming `ledger_id` exists, now check:\n\n**Check 2a: Is it unique?**\n\n- Query profile data for `ledger_id` column\n- Check: duplicate_count == 0?\n- If duplicates exist → **Warning** (not blocker): \"This column has 150 duplicate values. Are you sure it's a primary key?\"\n\n**Check 2b: Does it have nulls?**\n\n- Check: null_count == 0?\n- If nulls exist → **Warning**: \"This column has 25 NULL values. Primary keys typically shouldn't have NULLs.\"\n\n**Check 2c: Data type appropriateness**\n\n- Is it INTEGER/BIGINT/UUID/VARCHAR? (typical PK types)\n- If it's FLOAT/TEXT/JSON → **Warning**: \"Unusual data type for primary key\"\n\n**User Decision Point**:\n\n- Accept warnings and proceed\n- Go back and reconsider\n- Request more information about why this matters\n\n---\n\n### **Layer 3: Semantic Validation** (Ring 3 - Quality)\n\nFor free-text fields (like relationship descriptions):\n\n**If user modified description** from:\n\n- Old: \"Links general ledger entries to account codes\"\n- New: \"asdfgh\"\n\n**Validation Checks**:\n\n1. **Length check**: Min 10 chars? ❌ Fail\n2. **Gibberish detection**: High entropy, no recognizable words? ❌ Fail\n3. **Profanity filter**: Contains inappropriate words? ❌ Fail\n4. **LLM semantic check**: \"Is this a meaningful database relationship description?\"\n    - LLM response: \"No, this appears to be random characters\"\n    - ❌ Fail\n\n**Outcome**: Block with message \"Please provide a meaningful description of the relationship\"\n","x":-1360,"y":340,"width":620,"height":490},
		{"id":"3a4fb93fa55bb554","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 1: Discovery & Identification**\n\n### User Entry Point\n\nUser is browsing metadata UI and sees:\n\n```\nTable: GENERAL_LEDGER\nPrimary Key: line_unique_key (inferred by AI)\nConfidence: 87%\nStatus: Pending Review\n```\n\n**User Reaction**: \"This is wrong! The primary key should be `ledger_id`\"\n\n**System State**:\n\n- LLM has generated embeddings based on `line_unique_key` being PK\n- Relationships may reference this column\n- Source-level metadata aggregates this information\n- Other tables may have FKs pointing to it\n\n","x":-2740,"y":340,"width":620,"height":490},
		{"id":"a82181b8db4fecc4","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 2: User Initiates Correction**\n\n### User Action\n\nClicks \"Edit\" → Changes `line_unique_key` to `ledger_id`\n\n### System Pre-Save Checks\n\nBefore accepting the input, system needs to know:\n\n**Validation Queue Trigger**:\n\n1. What type of field is being changed? (PK, FK, description, etc.)\n2. What's the validation ring level? (Physical reality, best practices, semantic quality)\n3. What's the blast radius? (Just this field, or cascading effects)\n","x":-2040,"y":340,"width":620,"height":490},
		{"id":"8258af5b53691255","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 6: Data State Transition**\n\n### Before Re-inference\n\n**Mark user correction**:\n\n```\nField: primary_keys\nOld Value: [\"line_unique_key\"]\nNew Value: [\"ledger_id\"]\nSource: \"human\"\nValidated By: user_123\nValidated At: 2026-01-16T10:30:00Z\nValidation Status: \"approved\"\nLocked: true (prevent auto-override)\nChange Reason: \"User correction - original inference was incorrect\"\n```\n\n**Flag affected items**:\n\n```\nTable GENERAL_LEDGER:\n  Status: \"re_inference_queued\"\n  Reason: \"PK changed by user\"\n  \nRelationship R1, R2, R3:\n  Status: \"needs_review\"\n  Reason: \"Parent table PK changed\"\n```\n","x":-1360,"y":860,"width":620,"height":560},
		{"id":"7b047b5efcba79e8","type":"text","text":"\n## **Phase 5: User Decision & Approval**\n\n### Approval Workflow Options\n\n**Option A: Single Approval**\n\n- Show full impact report\n- Single button: \"Apply Changes & Re-infer\"\n- User trusts the system to handle everything\n\n**Option B: Granular Approval**\n\n- Show impact by category\n- User can selectively approve:\n    - ✅ Yes, update table metadata\n    - ✅ Yes, update relationships\n    - ❌ No, don't touch source metadata yet (I'll review manually)\n\n**Option C: Async Approval**\n\n- Accept correction immediately\n- Re-inference happens in background\n- User gets notification when complete: \"Review 15 updated items\"\n- User can approve/reject each change\n\n**Decision Point**: Which option based on:\n\n- Scope of change (1 field vs 100 fields)\n- User expertise (DBA vs business analyst)\n- Risk tolerance (development vs production)\n","x":-2040,"y":860,"width":620,"height":560},
		{"id":"92844f01c54ed968","type":"text","text":"\n## **Phase 4: Impact Analysis**\n\nUser's correction has passed validation. Now calculate ripple effects.\n\n### Impact Discovery Algorithm\n\n**Starting Point**: User changed PK from `line_unique_key` → `ledger_id`\n\n**What needs checking?**\n\n**Level 1 - Direct Dependencies**:\n\n1. **Table embedding_input**: Mentions old PK in description → Needs regeneration\n2. **Relationships where this table is parent**: Any FKs pointing to old column → Need review\n3. **Relationships where this table is child**: Does this affect understanding? → Maybe regenerate descriptions\n\n**Level 2 - Indirect Dependencies**:\n\n1. **Source embedding_input**: Aggregates all table info → Needs regeneration\n2. **Other tables with FKs**: If they reference this table → Validate FK still points correctly\n3. **Query patterns**: If stored query examples reference old PK → Flag for review\n\n**Level 3 - Business Logic**:\n\n1. **Dashboards/Reports**: Do any reference this metadata? → Flag for user notification\n2. **Data lineage**: Does this affect downstream understanding? → Recalculate lineage\n3. **User-saved searches**: Embeddings might no longer match → May need re-indexing\n\n### Impact Report Generation\n\nSystem generates preview:\n\n```\nYour change will affect:\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n✓ 1 Table metadata (GENERAL_LEDGER)\n✓ 3 Foreign key relationships \n✓ 1 Source metadata (Finance DB)\n✓ 12 Column descriptions (need re-inference)\n⚠ 2 Saved queries (may need update)\n\nEstimated re-inference time: ~45 seconds\n```\n","x":-2740,"y":860,"width":620,"height":560},
		{"id":"07ffe040b00d713e","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 9: Conflict Detection & Resolution**\n\n### What if re-inference contradicts user input?\n\n**Scenario**:\n\n- User said: `ledger_id` is PK\n- After re-inference, LLM analyzing profile data suggests: \"Actually, `ledger_id` has duplicates, recommended composite key: [`ledger_id`, `entry_date`]\"\n\n**Conflict Resolution Options**:\n\n**Option A: Human Always Wins**\n\n- Keep user's choice\n- Flag LLM suggestion as \"alternative consideration\"\n- Log disagreement for later analysis\n\n**Option B: Present Conflict to User**\n\n- \"We found something interesting during re-analysis...\"\n- Show both perspectives\n- Let user decide with full context\n\n**Option C: Confidence-Based**\n\n- If LLM high confidence (>90%) → Flag for review\n- If LLM low confidence (<50%) → Accept user input silently\n- Middle ground → Show as suggestion","x":-1360,"y":1480,"width":620,"height":549},
		{"id":"b1aaca44082e8f1c","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 8: Change Review & Confirmation**\n\n### Present Changes to User\n\n**Show diff view**:\n\n```\nGENERAL_LEDGER Table\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nPrimary Key:\n  - line_unique_key (AI)\n  + ledger_id (You) ✓\n\nEmbedding Changed:\n  Before: \"Table tracks ledger lines with unique key line_unique_key...\"\n  After:  \"Table tracks ledger entries identified by ledger_id...\"\n  \nRelationships Updated: 3\n  → TRANSACTIONS.ledger_line_id → GENERAL_LEDGER.ledger_id\n     Description updated: \"Foreign key reference to ledger entry\"\n     \n  → ACCOUNTS.related_ledger_id → GENERAL_LEDGER.ledger_id\n     Description updated: \"Links account to general ledger via ledger_id\"\n     \n  → AUDIT_LOG.source_ledger_id → GENERAL_LEDGER.ledger_id\n     ⚠ Warning: FK column datatype is VARCHAR, PK is INTEGER\n     \nSource Metadata:\n  Finance DB embedding regenerated\n```\n\n### User Actions\n\n- **Accept All**: Trust the re-inference\n- **Review Each**: Go through item by item\n- **Reject & Rollback**: \"Actually, the AI was right\"\n- **Partial Accept**: Accept some changes, reject others","x":-2060,"y":1480,"width":620,"height":560},
		{"id":"5bc13970672987c9","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 7: Re-inference Execution**\n\n### Sequential Re-inference Pipeline\n\n**Stage 1: Column-Level Re-inference**\n\n- `ledger_id` column: Update embedding_input to reflect it's now the PK\n- Profile data: May need recomputation (uniqueness stats, cardinality)\n- Related columns: FK columns pointing here → validate still compatible\n\n**Stage 2: Table-Level Re-inference**\n\n- Regenerate table embedding_input:\n    - Input to LLM: Table structure with NEW PK\n    - Prompt: \"Generate a comprehensive description of this table, noting that ledger_id is the primary key\"\n- Recalculate relationships:\n    - For each FK relationship, verify column datatypes still match\n    - Regenerate relationship descriptions considering new PK\n\n**Stage 3: Source-Level Re-inference**\n\n- Aggregate all table information (with updated GENERAL_LEDGER metadata)\n- Regenerate source embedding_input\n- Update source-level statistics\n\n**Stage 4: Cross-Entity Validation**\n\n- Run consistency checks across all three levels\n- Detect orphaned relationships\n- Identify embedding conflicts\n\n### Re-inference Strategies\n\n**Strategy A: Full Re-generation**\n\n- Regenerate everything from scratch\n- Safest but slowest\n- Use when: Major structural change\n\n**Strategy B: Incremental Update**\n\n- Only regenerate embeddings that mention the changed field\n- Use NLP to detect mentions in existing embeddings\n- Faster but might miss subtle dependencies\n\n**Strategy C: Hybrid**\n\n- Critical fields (PK, FK) → Full regeneration\n- Descriptions, comments → Incremental update\n- Balance between thoroughness and performance","x":-2740,"y":1480,"width":620,"height":560},
		{"id":"233be1b7c2ee3cbd","type":"text","text":"## **Key Open Questions**\n\n1. **How many steps should require explicit user approval?** Too many = friction, too few = lack of control\n2. **What's the threshold for \"significant impact\"?** 3 affected items? 50? 1000?\n3. **Should validation rules differ by user role?** Admin vs analyst vs viewer\n4. **How to handle \"tentative\" corrections?** Can users mark something as \"I think this is right but not sure\"\n5. **Versioning strategy**: Do you keep history of all changes? For how long?","x":-1360,"y":2080,"width":620,"height":560},
		{"id":"4666b0b30d994aab","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 11: Edge Cases & Error Handling**\n\n### What can go wrong?\n\n**Scenario A: Re-inference Fails**\n\n- LLM timeout, API error, embedding service down\n- **Fallback**: Keep user correction, mark re-inference as \"pending retry\"\n- Don't block user, retry asynchronously\n\n**Scenario B: Cascading Conflicts**\n\n- Fixing one thing breaks another\n- Example: New PK makes 5 FK relationships invalid\n- **Resolution**: Present as bulk decision: \"Accept all changes, or revert\"\n\n**Scenario C: Concurrent Edits**\n\n- User A changes PK while User B is updating relationship description\n- **Locking mechanism needed**:\n    - Optimistic: Let both proceed, detect conflict, last-write-wins with notification\n    - Pessimistic: Lock entity during editing, queue other users\n\n**Scenario D: Schema Drift**\n\n- User correction based on v1 schema, but production is on v2\n- **Version tracking needed**: Tag metadata with schema version\n\n---\n\n## **Critical Decision Points Summary**\n\nThroughout this flow, you need to decide:\n\n1. **Validation Strictness**: Block vs Warn vs Allow for each ring level\n2. **Approval Granularity**: Bulk accept vs review each item\n3. **Re-inference Timing**: Real-time vs async vs batch\n4. **Conflict Resolution**: Human-first vs AI-first vs collaborative\n5. **Rollback Strategy**: Full revert vs partial vs forward-only\n6. **Performance Trade-offs**: Thoroughness vs speed\n7. **User Communication**: How much detail to show at each step","x":-2040,"y":2080,"width":620,"height":560},
		{"id":"2691b73a24836ae1","type":"text","text":"## **Phase 10: Finalization & Monitoring**\n\n### Post-Acceptance Actions\n\n**Immediate**:\n\n- Remove \"re_inference_queued\" status flags\n- Mark all entities as \"validated\"\n- Update search indices with new embeddings\n- Notify affected users (if collaborative environment)\n\n**Short-term**:\n\n- Monitor query performance (do searches still work well?)\n- Track user satisfaction (do they make further corrections?)\n- Log correction patterns (is LLM consistently wrong on certain types?)\n\n**Long-term**:\n\n- Feed corrections back into LLM training examples\n- Adjust inference confidence models\n- Identify systematic issues (e.g., always wrong about PKs in certain schemas)","x":-2740,"y":2080,"width":620,"height":560}
	],
